<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa/southern Minnesota hog receipts Monday were 100,000 head, compared with no receipts during last week's Memorial Day holiday and 80,000 last year, USDA said.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts steady to firm compared to midsession Friday. Trade slow for moderate demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    53.00 -54.50	   54.00 -55.50</p>
<p>Liberal volume	 54.00 -54.50	   54.50 -55.50</p>
<p>few			55.00		    56.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    52.00 -54.50	   52.50 -55.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    52.00 -54.50	   52.50 -55.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to $1.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  43.00 -46.00	   44.00 -47.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -47.00	   45.00 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    46.00 -48.00	   47.00 -49.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
